From 5cd32d392b1e4d882e8da32b3ee7b8e379e21a83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saulo Vallory <me@saulo.engineer>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 21:07:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat: base position for parseMarko to support offset fragment
 parsing

Config.htmlParseOptions gains startOffset/startLine/startColumn. When
given, parseMarko threads them through htmljs-parser's own new parse()
base-position option (see the paired htmljs-parser patch) so every
node's start/end/loc and every thrown SyntaxError's position come out
relative to an enclosing document instead of the substring passed as
code. Uses htmljs-parser's positionAt/locationAt/offsetAt as the single
translation points; loc.js's getLoc/getLocRange/withLoc (used by the
Babel sub-parse for expressions, params, etc.) apply the same base.
Absent the option, behavior is unchanged.

Numeric start/end are shifted once, in a single walk, right after
parsing finishes -- not per-node during it, which would double-shift
a tag's start/end when onCloseTagEnd's locationAt(node) reads them
back mid-parse as if still fragment-relative. loc (line/column)
already comes out correct at the source via the patched
positionAt/locationAt.

Local dev note: verifying this against a linked, patched htmljs-parser
requires 'pnpm link ../htmljs-parser' run manually after install --
do NOT add a pnpm-workspace.yaml override or edit pnpm-lock.yaml for
this, since a lockfile relock here changes @marko/runtime-tags
resolution from this monorepo's own workspace package to the
published npm version, which fails 29 unrelated tests for reasons
having nothing to do with this patch (confirmed: getFile() throws
inside a runtime-tags migrator during compileFile, reproducible with
this patch fully reverted, purely from the resolution change).
